course: everyday
lesson: 405
title: Teams and voice chat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Leo, Kai and Priya joined a Fortnite squad from three different houses, and for the first five minutes all three talked at once: «Where are we landing — no, LEFT — who's got shield — wait, I'm stuck in a bush.» They were knocked out before they'd found a single chest. Next game Priya said, «One at a time. Short. Say where, then what.» «Enemy, blue house, two of them.» They lasted twice as long.
explain: Then Ollie forgot his mic was on. The whole squad heard his mum, from the bottom of the stairs, at full volume: «OLLIE! YOUR TEA! I WILL NOT SAY IT AGAIN!» Followed by Ollie whispering, «Mum, I'm LIVE.» Kai laughed so much he fell off his beanbag. Meanwhile Zara played the whole evening whispering, because her baby brother was asleep next door — and her whispered «there's one behind you» was somehow the scariest thing anyone heard all night.
explain: Downstairs at Priya's, her dad heard her shouting, «PUSH, PUSH, they're one shot, FINISH THEM!» and ran up the stairs thinking something terrible was happening. «It's a GAME, Dad.» «One shot means one hit from being knocked out,» she explained, in the voice of someone explaining something obvious to a very old person. He went back down to his tea, shaking his head. Gaming talk sounds alarming to people who don't know it.
explain: Teams go wrong in funny ways too. Mia's squad kept losing because all four of them wanted to be the sniper and nobody wanted to heal anyone. In Minecraft, Ruby built an entire castle with towers while Theo «helped» by digging holes, one of which Ruby fell into. Jayden played Dota 2 with his older cousin, was handed a hero he barely knew, and spent the match apologising to four strangers on the team. Leo said «my bad» after every single mistake until Kai said, «Mate, stop saying my bad and just keep playing.»
explain: And then there was Noah's team captain, a boy from the year above who shouted orders like a general: «You, there! You, go! Why are you so useless?» It stopped being fun. Kai, meanwhile, only ever plays with friends he knows in real life and refuses to join random squads: «I don't know who they are, so no.» Good teams share jobs, take turns, talk clearly and kindly, and laugh at the tea moments. A bossy captain isn't a good one, and you are allowed to leave a game that has stopped being fun.
fact: When everyone talks at once on voice chat, nobody can understand anything.
fact: Short, clear messages that say where and what help a team most.
fact: A microphone left on can let everyone in the game hear what is happening in your home.
fact: Most consoles and games let you mute your microphone and let parents limit voice chat to friends.
fact: Playing only with people you know in real life is safer than joining strangers.
fact: Game slang such as «push» and «one shot» can sound frightening to people who do not play.
fact: A good team shares out jobs instead of everyone wanting the same one.
fact: Saying sorry once for a mistake is kind; saying it after every mistake can distract the team.
fact: A good leader gives clear instructions politely and does not insult players.
fact: You can leave a game or a group if someone is being nasty, and tell an adult if it keeps happening.
exercise: Why did Leo, Kai and Priya lose the first game so fast? | They all talked at once and nobody understood | Their internet was too slow that evening | They all landed in the sea and drowned | They forgot to press start
exercise: What was Priya's rule for talking? | One at a time, short, say where then what | Everyone shout louder so the whole team hears you | Only Priya may talk, the rest just listen | Talk in a secret code
exercise: Which message is most useful to a team? | «Enemy, blue house, two of them» | «Oh no oh no oh no, they're everywhere» | «Something's happening somewhere» | «Guys guys guys guys»
exercise: What did the squad hear because Ollie's mic was on? | His mum shouting about his tea | His dog barking along to the game music | The doorbell ringing | His sister singing in the bath
exercise: What could Ollie have done to avoid it? | Muted his mic when not talking | Turned the game volume right up to the top | Played in the garden | Asked his mum to whisper from now on
exercise: Why was Zara whispering? | Her baby brother was asleep | She had lost her voice from shouting at school | She was playing a stealth game | She was scared of her own team
exercise: Why did Priya's dad run upstairs? | Game talk like «finish them» sounded alarming | He wanted to have a go on the game too | He heard the console fall off the shelf and break | Tea was ready
exercise: What does «one shot» mean in the game? | One hit from being knocked out | One person left alive in the whole world | Only one bullet allowed per round | A photo of the screen at the end
exercise: Why did Mia's squad keep losing? | Everyone wanted the same job and nobody healed | They had no sniper at all in the whole squad | They played too carefully all game | They were too good
exercise: What went wrong with Ruby and Theo in Minecraft? | Ruby did all the building while Theo dug holes | Theo built a much better castle and Ruby got jealous | Ruby dug all the holes | They built two castles each
exercise: Why did Jayden keep apologising in Dota 2? | He didn't know his hero well | His cousin made him say it after every fight | The game asks you to say sorry | He was winning far too easily
exercise: Why did Kai tell Leo to stop saying «my bad»? | Saying it every time was distracting the team | Leo wasn't allowed to talk on voice chat | «My bad» is a rude thing to say in games | Leo had done nothing wrong ever
exercise: What was wrong with Noah's team captain? | He shouted orders and insulted people | He was far too quiet to hear | He let everyone choose what to do, so nobody did anything | He kept saying sorry
exercise: Why does Kai only play with real-life friends? | He knows who they are, which is safer | Strangers are always better players | Random squads cost money to join | His console can't join randoms
exercise: What can you do if a team captain keeps being nasty? | Leave the game and tell an adult if it continues | Shout back louder | Keep playing and say nothing forever | Give him your password to calm him down
exercise: What kind of courage is saying «let's take turns being sniper»? | Speaking up kindly to make it fair | Grabbing the sniper first before anyone else can | Quitting without a word | Making everyone else heal instead
test: «WHERE R WE LANDING NO LEFT NO WAIT IM IN A BUSH». What would help most? | One person talks at a time, short and clear | Everyone shouts even louder so they get heard | Turning off the game | Nobody says anything at all
test: «OLLIE YOUR TEA» lol the whole squad heard. What's the lesson? | Mute your mic when you're not talking | Tell your mum to never call you while you play | Never eat tea while gaming | Play with the sound off
test: «push push they're one shot!» Dad's at the door, white as a sheet. What does Priya mean? | Attack, the enemy is nearly knocked out | Someone in the house is really badly hurt | She's pushing her little brother off the sofa | She's taking a photo
test: «all 4 of us went sniper again and lost AGAIN». What should the squad do? | Share out the jobs, including healing | Pick snipers harder and aim better next time | Play without any plan at all | Blame the game
test: «ruby built everything, theo dug holes, then she fell in one lol». Fair team? | No, a team shares the work | Yes, holes are important too | Yes, Ruby likes building alone | No, Theo should build everything
test: «random squad wants me in, they seem sound, join?» What would Kai say? | No, play with people you know in real life | Yes, everyone online is nice | Yes, and give them your real name so they trust you | Only if they're good
test: «captain keeps calling me useless». Best move? | Leave the game and tell an adult if it continues | Call him worse names | Keep quiet and keep playing for hours and hours | Send him your password to be friends
test: «my bad. my bad. MY BAD.» Leo's said it 30 times. What helps? | Say sorry once and keep playing | Say it louder so they really hear it | Quit every time he makes a mistake | Never speak again for the whole game
test: «jayden's cousin gave him a hero he's never played, lol». What's a sensible thing for Jayden to say? | «I don't know this one, any quick tips?» | Nothing, and pretend he's an expert at it | «This game is stupid» and leave | «It's your fault if we lose»
test: «zara's whispering on chat, so creepy». Why is she? | Her baby brother is asleep | She's hiding from the police | She's been told off for shouting | Whispering makes you play better
test: Teacher: «What makes a good team in an online game?» | Clear talk, shared jobs and kindness | One person giving all the orders to the rest | Everyone doing the same job | Shouting so the enemy hears
exam: Identify the form of communication most conducive to effective co-ordination within a team in an online game. | Brief statements issued in turn, specifying location and circumstance | Simultaneous exclamations by all members of the team | Prolonged silence on the part of every member | Repeated apologies following every error
exam: Ascertain the principal hazard arising from a microphone which is inadvertently left active during play. | Persons in the game may overhear what occurs within the player's home | The console may be permanently damaged by the continuous use of the microphone | The game may be terminated by its publisher | The player's score may be reduced
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the conduct of a competent team leader? | Instructions are given clearly and courteously, without insult to any player | Instructions are shouted loudly and accompanied by insults to the weaker players | Every decision is withheld from the team | All tasks are allocated to the leader alone
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning participation in online games with unknown persons. | Play with persons known in real life is the safer course | Unknown persons are invariably trustworthy and well-intentioned | Unknown persons must be given personal details | Play with unknown persons is required by the game
